'' FB.Array( of T ) as a TYPE FIELD, used from the owner's own methods.
''
'' No golden: the IR differs between the two targets once fb/array.bi is in it. The
'' assertions below are the property, not the shape.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/mir/src/generic-field-container.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' A FIELD CALL BINDS TO THE INSTANTIATION'S MEMBER, named for its argument. The
'' generic's own members are never lowered -- their parameters are void and their
'' fields have no offsets -- so a call left bound to one is a call to nothing.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN5ArrayIhE4PUSHERh(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN5ArrayI8FBSTRINGE4PUSHERS0_(

'' A CONTAINER OF A TYPE THAT ITSELF HOLDS CONTAINERS.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN5ArrayI3BUFE4PUSHERS0_(

'' 'for each' over a FIELD: GetIterator comes back typed, so the loop lowers. The
'' CALL is not spelled the same on both targets -- a 16-byte return is an sret
'' pointer under win64 and a register pair under SysV -- so the assertion is the
'' NAME, which is the instantiation's.
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN5ArrayIhE11GETITERATOREv(
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
